<article class="env-lemma" id="0BM4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BM4">Lemma <span data-tag="0BM4">15.24.20</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian normal domain with fraction field $K$. Let $L$ be a finite extension of $K$. If the integral closure $B$ of $A$ in $L$ is finite over $A$, then $B$ is reflexive as an $A$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It suffices to show that $B = \bigcap B_\mathfrak p$ where the intersection is over height $1$ primes $\mathfrak p \subset A$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0AVB" data-tag="0AVB">15.24.18</a>. Let $b \in \bigcap B_\mathfrak p$. Let $x^ d + a_1x^{d - 1} + \ldots + a_ d$ be the minimal polynomial of $b$ over $K$. We want to show $a_ i \in A$. By Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00H7" data-tag="00H7">10.38.6</a> we see that $a_ i \in A_\mathfrak p$ for all $i$ and all height one primes $\mathfrak p$. Hence we get what we want from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031T" data-tag="031T">10.157.6</a> (or the lemma already cited as $A$ is a reflexive module over itself). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>